From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: let a supplicant see an offloaded key exchange

An offloaded frame is delivered on the virtual device's network device and
never enters mac80211, so the control port mac80211 offers over netlink
carries nothing once the NSS firmware owns the data path. A supplicant that
takes the offer stops reading the interface, and the key exchange it is
waiting for arrives somewhere it is no longer looking: no station reaches
authorised, whatever the firmware does with the frames.

The capability is a wiphy feature bit and mac80211 sets it for every driver,
so it is withdrawn here rather than in mac80211, and only while the offload
is on. A supplicant then falls back to the interface itself, which is where
the frames are.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
---
Index: backports-6.18.39/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
===================================================================
--- backports-6.18.39.orig/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
+++ backports-6.18.39/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
@@ -10470,7 +10470,26 @@ static int __ath11k_mac_register(struct
 	    ab->hw_params.bios_sar_capa)
 		ar->hw->wiphy->sar_capa = ab->hw_params.bios_sar_capa;
 
+	/* Before registration, because the capability is read off the wiphy
+	 * once it is published.
+	 */
+	if (ath11k_nss_offload) {
+		static const enum nl80211_ext_feature_index over_nl[] = {
+			NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_CONTROL_PORT_OVER_NL80211,
+			NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_CONTROL_PORT_NO_PREAUTH,
+			NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_CONTROL_PORT_OVER_NL80211_TX_STATUS,
+		};
+		struct wiphy *wiphy = ar->hw->wiphy;
+		int f;
+
+		for (f = 0; f < ARRAY_SIZE(over_nl); f++) {
+			enum nl80211_ext_feature_index ft = over_nl[f];
+
+			wiphy->ext_features[ft / 8] &= ~BIT(ft % 8);
+		}
+	}
+
 	ret = ieee80211_register_hw(ar->hw);
 	if (ret) {
 		ath11k_err(ar->ab, "ieee80211 registration failed: %d\n", ret);
